  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting Adolescent Girls against Violence in Humanitarian Settings: Joint Programming on Safe Spaces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved prevention of and response to violence against adolescent girls in humanitarian settings, particularly in Ethiopia, Pakistan and DRC by providing adolescent girls and their communities with the skills and knowledge needed to lessen their risk to violence. This will directly benefit 8615 adolescent girls and will also provide a platform for learning and dissemination of knowledge on this under-developed area of work. This contributes to our MDG&#x2019;s by improving prevention of and response to violence against women and girls and will result in X% (yet to be established) of girls feeling safer in their environments by 2016.</narrative>
  </description>
